{"version":"0.1.0","operators":[{"id":"thin-film-interference","title":"Thin-film interference","family":"interference","reusable":true,"description":"Two-interface Airy interference. Color is a function of optical path 2 n d cos θ, not a material flag. Oil slicks, soap films, oxide tarnish, and lacquered foil all bind this operator.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"references":["Heavens 1955","Belcour & Barla 2017"],"slots":{"thickness":{"kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","required":true,"field":"required"},"nIncident":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"nFilm":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"nExit":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"multilayer-interference","title":"Multilayer interference","family":"interference","reusable":true,"description":"N-period Bragg / lamellar stack. Peak wavelength is set by bilayer optical thickness and IOR contrast. Nacre, labradorite, and Morpho-type scales share this operator.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"references":["Kinoshita 2008","Nassau 2001"],"slots":{"layerCount":{"kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"thicknessA":{"kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"thicknessB":{"kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"nA":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"nB":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"orientation":{"kind":"angle","unit":"rad","required":true,"field":"required"}}},{"id":"diffraction-grating","title":"Diffraction grating","family":"diffraction","reusable":true,"description":"Periodic microstructure. The grating equation m λ = p (sin θi + sin θd) produces spectral orders. Butterfly scale ridges and embossed holographic foil bind the same operator with different periods.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"references":["Born & Wolf","Kinoshita 2008"],"slots":{"period":{"kind":"period","unit":"um","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"depth":{"kind":"length","unit":"nm","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"orientation":{"kind":"angle","unit":"rad","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"orders":{"kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"fresnel-dielectric","title":"Dielectric Fresnel","family":"interface","reusable":true,"description":"Real-IOR interface reflectance (Schlick / exact Fresnel). Used wherever a dielectric boundary is visible: films, nacre, water, glass.","outputs":["bsdf-lobe","weight"],"slots":{"ior":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"fresnel-conductor","title":"Conductor Fresnel","family":"interface","reusable":true,"description":"Complex-IOR interface for metals. n and k may be spectral. Foil aluminum, bismuth, and molten chrome share this operator.","outputs":["bsdf-lobe"],"slots":{"ior":{"kind":"ior-complex","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"microfacet-scatter","title":"Microfacet scatter","family":"interface","reusable":true,"description":"GGX/Beckmann distribution of normals. Roughness and anisotropy are geometric, independent of the Fresnel term they modulate.","outputs":["bsdf-lobe"],"slots":{"roughness":{"kind":"roughness","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"anisotropy":{"kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"allowed"}}},{"id":"refraction-snell","title":"Snell refraction","family":"geometric","reusable":true,"description":"Transmission through a dielectric interface. eta is the relative IOR. Water and bulk glass both bind this operator.","outputs":["throughput"],"slots":{"iorInside":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"iorOutside":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"caustic-transport","title":"Caustic transport","family":"geometric","reusable":true,"description":"Focusing of refracted or reflected light by a displacement field. Intensity follows the inverse Jacobian of the refracted mapping. Water surfaces are the type specimen; oil on waves reuses it.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"slots":{"displacement":{"kind":"length","unit":"mm","required":true,"field":"required"},"ior":{"kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"focusScale":{"kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"volume-scattering","title":"Volume scattering","family":"volume","reusable":true,"description":"In-scattering with a closed phase-function enum (Henyey-Greenstein, Rayleigh, Mie). Cloud, nebula, and opalescent glass differ by density, albedo, and phase — not by separate operators.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"slots":{"density":{"kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","required":true,"field":"required"},"sigmaS":{"kind":"scattering-coeff","unit":"1/m","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"phase":{"kind":"phase-function","unit":"enum","required":true,"field":"forbidden","enumValues":["hg","rayleigh","mie"]},"g":{"kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","required":false,"field":"forbidden","notes":"Used when phase is hg or mie."}}},{"id":"volume-absorption","title":"Volume absorption","family":"volume","reusable":true,"description":"Beer-Lambert extinction. sigmaA may be spectral (water red-absorb, nebular dust). Shared by participating media and tinted dielectrics.","outputs":["throughput"],"slots":{"density":{"kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","required":true,"field":"required"},"sigmaA":{"kind":"extinction","unit":"1/m","required":true,"field":"allowed"}}},{"id":"volume-emission","title":"Volume emission","family":"volume","reusable":true,"description":"Additive spectral emission in a medium or at a hot surface treated as a thin emitting layer. Nebular lines and molten-metal blackbody both bind this operator.","outputs":["spectral-radiance"],"slots":{"density":{"kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","required":true,"field":"allowed"},"radiance":{"kind":"spectral-power","unit":"W/m3/sr/nm","required":false,"field":"allowed"},"temperature":{"kind":"temperature","unit":"K","required":false,"field":"forbidden"}}},{"id":"view-dependent-weight","title":"View-dependent weight","family":"evaluation","reusable":true,"description":"Weights upstream radiance by a viewing/lighting lobe (fresnel, grazing, retro, specular). Structural color is directional because of this operator, not because of a material-named anisotropic flag.","outputs":["weight"],"slots":{"exponent":{"kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","required":true,"field":"forbidden"},"lobe":{"kind":"lobe","unit":"enum","required":true,"field":"forbidden","enumValues":["fresnel","grazing","retro","specular"]}}},{"id":"spectral-integrate","title":"Spectral integrate","family":"evaluation","reusable":true,"description":"Converts spectral radiance to display RGB under a standard illuminant and observer. Every colored recipe ends here so that encoding stays spectral until evaluation.","outputs":["display-rgb"],"slots":{"illuminant":{"kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","required":true,"field":"forbidden","enumValues":["D65","A","E"]},"observer":{"kind":"observer","unit":"enum","required":true,"field":"forbidden","enumValues":["CIE-1931-2deg"]}}}],"recipes":[{"id":"bismuth-oxide","version":"0.1.0","title":"Bismuth oxide","taxonomyIds":["thin-film","conductor-interface","microfacet"],"summary":"An oxide film on bismuth metal. Iridescent tarnish is thin-film interference against a conductor Fresnel exit medium, with hopper-crystal roughness — the same film operator as oil and soap.","phenomena":["thin-film-interference","conductor-fresnel"],"fields":[{"id":"oxide-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"worley","frequency":4.5},"range":[40,380],"notes":"Oxidation fronts follow hopper steps, so thickness is cellular rather than smoothly fbm."},{"id":"hopper-roughness","kind":"roughness","unit":"dimensionless","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"worley","frequency":3.2},"range":[0.08,0.45]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-air","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.0003},{"id":"n-oxide","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":2.15,"range":[1.9,2.5]},{"id":"n-exit-proxy","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.8,"notes":"Real part of the metal used as film exit IOR; the conductor node carries the complex pair."},{"id":"ior-bismuth","kind":"ior-complex","unit":"dimensionless","complex":{"n":1.8,"k":3.4}},{"id":"anisotropy","kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.15},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"oxide","operator":"thin-film-interference","bind":{"thickness":{"field":"oxide-thickness"},"nIncident":{"param":"n-air"},"nFilm":{"param":"n-oxide"},"nExit":{"param":"n-exit-proxy"}}},{"id":"metal","operator":"fresnel-conductor","bind":{"ior":{"param":"ior-bismuth"}}},{"id":"microfacet","operator":"microfacet-scatter","bind":{"roughness":{"field":"hopper-roughness"},"anisotropy":{"param":"anisotropy"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"oxide","to":"display"},{"from":"metal","to":"microfacet"},{"from":"microfacet","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"butterfly-structural-color","version":"0.1.0","title":"Butterfly structural color","taxonomyIds":["multilayer","grating","view-weight"],"summary":"Chitin scale architecture: a multilayer stack for the Bragg peak plus a ridge grating for angular selectivity. Morpho-type blue is composed, not a named morpho shader.","phenomena":["multilayer-interference","diffraction","view-dependent-color"],"fields":[{"id":"scale-orientation","kind":"angle","unit":"rad","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"anisotropic-orientation","frequency":8},"range":[-0.12,0.12]},{"id":"ridge-period","kind":"period","unit":"um","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":2,"frequency":12},"range":[0.6,1.1]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-chitin","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.56},{"id":"n-air-gap","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1},{"id":"lamella-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","value":90},{"id":"gap-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","value":70},{"id":"layer-count","kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","value":10},{"id":"groove-depth","kind":"length","unit":"nm","value":220},{"id":"orders","kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","value":3},{"id":"view-exp","kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","value":6},{"id":"view-lobe","kind":"lobe","unit":"enum","enum":"specular"},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"stack","operator":"multilayer-interference","bind":{"layerCount":{"param":"layer-count"},"thicknessA":{"param":"lamella-thickness"},"thicknessB":{"param":"gap-thickness"},"nA":{"param":"n-chitin"},"nB":{"param":"n-air-gap"},"orientation":{"field":"scale-orientation"}}},{"id":"ridges","operator":"diffraction-grating","bind":{"period":{"field":"ridge-period"},"depth":{"param":"groove-depth"},"orientation":{"field":"scale-orientation"},"orders":{"param":"orders"}}},{"id":"view","operator":"view-dependent-weight","bind":{"exponent":{"param":"view-exp"},"lobe":{"param":"view-lobe"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"stack","to":"view"},{"from":"ridges","to":"view"},{"from":"view","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"caustic-water","version":"0.1.0","title":"Caustic water","taxonomyIds":["refraction","caustics","dielectric-interface","absorption"],"summary":"A dielectric water surface. Caustics are Snell refraction composed with caustic transport of a displacement field; red-preferring absorption tints the volume. No water shader type.","phenomena":["refraction","caustics","dielectric-fresnel","spectral-absorption"],"fields":[{"id":"surface-displacement","kind":"length","unit":"mm","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"analytic","generator":"surface-waves","frequency":1.1},"range":[-24,24]},{"id":"volume-density","kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","domain":"volume","source":{"type":"constant","generator":"constant","value":1000},"range":[997,1025]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-air","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.0003},{"id":"n-water","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.333},{"id":"focus-scale","kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.4},{"id":"sigma-a","kind":"extinction","unit":"1/m","spectral":{"wavelengthsNm":[450,550,650],"samples":[0.02,0.06,0.35]},"notes":"Water absorbs red more than blue."},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"refract","operator":"refraction-snell","bind":{"iorInside":{"param":"n-water"},"iorOutside":{"param":"n-air"}}},{"id":"caustics","operator":"caustic-transport","bind":{"displacement":{"field":"surface-displacement"},"ior":{"param":"n-water"},"focusScale":{"param":"focus-scale"}}},{"id":"interface","operator":"fresnel-dielectric","bind":{"ior":{"param":"n-water"}}},{"id":"absorb","operator":"volume-absorption","bind":{"density":{"field":"volume-density"},"sigmaA":{"param":"sigma-a"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"refract","to":"caustics"},{"from":"caustics","to":"absorb"},{"from":"interface","to":"display"},{"from":"absorb","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"cloud","version":"0.1.0","title":"Cloud","taxonomyIds":["scattering","absorption"],"summary":"Water-droplet Mie scattering in a density field. White appearance is high albedo plus forward-peaked phase, not a cloud shader. Shares volume-scattering with nebula and opalescent glass.","phenomena":["mie-scattering","spectral-absorption"],"fields":[{"id":"droplet-density","kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","domain":"volume","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":5,"frequency":1.3},"range":[0,0.8]}],"parameters":[{"id":"sigma-s","kind":"scattering-coeff","unit":"1/m","value":12},{"id":"sigma-a","kind":"extinction","unit":"1/m","value":0.04},{"id":"phase","kind":"phase-function","unit":"enum","enum":"mie"},{"id":"g","kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.85,"notes":"Large droplets are strongly forward-scattering."},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"scatter","operator":"volume-scattering","bind":{"density":{"field":"droplet-density"},"sigmaS":{"param":"sigma-s"},"phase":{"param":"phase"},"g":{"param":"g"}}},{"id":"absorb","operator":"volume-absorption","bind":{"density":{"field":"droplet-density"},"sigmaA":{"param":"sigma-a"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"scatter","to":"display"},{"from":"absorb","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"holographic-foil","version":"0.1.0","title":"Holographic foil","taxonomyIds":["grating","thin-film","conductor-interface"],"summary":"Embossed PET over aluminum. Spectral orders come from the grating; a lacquer film adds Airy modulation; the metal is conductor Fresnel. No holographic boolean.","phenomena":["diffraction","thin-film-interference","conductor-fresnel"],"fields":[{"id":"groove-orientation","kind":"angle","unit":"rad","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"analytic","generator":"anisotropic-orientation","frequency":1},"range":[0,3.1416]},{"id":"lacquer-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":2,"frequency":5},"range":[180,420]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-air","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.0003},{"id":"n-pet","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.58},{"id":"n-lacquer","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.5},{"id":"period","kind":"period","unit":"um","value":0.85,"range":[0.5,1.6]},{"id":"groove-depth","kind":"length","unit":"nm","value":140},{"id":"orders","kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","value":4},{"id":"ior-aluminum","kind":"ior-complex","unit":"dimensionless","complex":{"n":0.9,"k":6.5},"notes":"Visible-band aluminum, approximate."},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"grating","operator":"diffraction-grating","bind":{"period":{"param":"period"},"depth":{"param":"groove-depth"},"orientation":{"field":"groove-orientation"},"orders":{"param":"orders"}}},{"id":"lacquer","operator":"thin-film-interference","bind":{"thickness":{"field":"lacquer-thickness"},"nIncident":{"param":"n-air"},"nFilm":{"param":"n-lacquer"},"nExit":{"param":"n-pet"}}},{"id":"metal","operator":"fresnel-conductor","bind":{"ior":{"param":"ior-aluminum"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"grating","to":"display"},{"from":"lacquer","to":"display"},{"from":"metal","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"labradorite","version":"0.1.0","title":"Labradorite","taxonomyIds":["multilayer","microfacet","view-weight"],"summary":"Exsolution lamellae in feldspar. Labradorescence is the same multilayer operator as nacre, with much lower IOR contrast, a tighter orientation field, and a microfacet envelope.","phenomena":["multilayer-interference","lamellar-flash","view-dependent-color"],"fields":[{"id":"lamellar-orientation","kind":"angle","unit":"rad","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"analytic","generator":"anisotropic-orientation","frequency":0.4},"range":[-0.08,0.08],"notes":"Flash occurs only when the viewing vector aligns with the lamellar normal."},{"id":"cleavage-roughness","kind":"roughness","unit":"dimensionless","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":2,"frequency":3},"range":[0.04,0.18]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-lamella-a","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.56},{"id":"n-lamella-b","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.53,"notes":"Δn ≈ 0.03 — enough for coherent interference, not a pigment."},{"id":"thickness-a","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","value":140},{"id":"thickness-b","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","value":120},{"id":"layer-count","kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","value":64},{"id":"anisotropy","kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.72},{"id":"view-exp","kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","value":8.5},{"id":"view-lobe","kind":"lobe","unit":"enum","enum":"specular"},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"stack","operator":"multilayer-interference","bind":{"layerCount":{"param":"layer-count"},"thicknessA":{"param":"thickness-a"},"thicknessB":{"param":"thickness-b"},"nA":{"param":"n-lamella-a"},"nB":{"param":"n-lamella-b"},"orientation":{"field":"lamellar-orientation"}}},{"id":"microfacet","operator":"microfacet-scatter","bind":{"roughness":{"field":"cleavage-roughness"},"anisotropy":{"param":"anisotropy"}}},{"id":"view","operator":"view-dependent-weight","bind":{"exponent":{"param":"view-exp"},"lobe":{"param":"view-lobe"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"stack","to":"view"},{"from":"microfacet","to":"view"},{"from":"view","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"molten-chrome","version":"0.1.0","title":"Molten chrome","taxonomyIds":["conductor-interface","microfacet","emission","view-weight"],"summary":"Liquid chromium: complex-IOR Fresnel, convection-driven roughness, and thermal emission. Heat is volume-emission with a blackbody temperature, not a moltenChrome flag.","phenomena":["conductor-fresnel","thermal-emission","view-dependent-color"],"fields":[{"id":"convection-roughness","kind":"roughness","unit":"dimensionless","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":5,"frequency":1.8},"range":[0.02,0.22]},{"id":"flow-anisotropy","kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"analytic","generator":"anisotropic-orientation","frequency":0.6},"range":[0.2,0.7]}],"parameters":[{"id":"ior-chrome","kind":"ior-complex","unit":"dimensionless","complex":{"n":3.2,"k":4.2}},{"id":"temperature","kind":"temperature","unit":"K","value":1900,"range":[1400,2200]},{"id":"emit-density","kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","value":1},{"id":"view-exp","kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","value":2},{"id":"view-lobe","kind":"lobe","unit":"enum","enum":"fresnel"},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"A"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"metal","operator":"fresnel-conductor","bind":{"ior":{"param":"ior-chrome"}}},{"id":"microfacet","operator":"microfacet-scatter","bind":{"roughness":{"field":"convection-roughness"},"anisotropy":{"field":"flow-anisotropy"}}},{"id":"heat","operator":"volume-emission","bind":{"density":{"param":"emit-density"},"temperature":{"param":"temperature"}}},{"id":"view","operator":"view-dependent-weight","bind":{"exponent":{"param":"view-exp"},"lobe":{"param":"view-lobe"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"metal","to":"microfacet"},{"from":"microfacet","to":"view"},{"from":"heat","to":"display"},{"from":"view","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"A","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"nacre","version":"0.1.0","title":"Nacre","taxonomyIds":["multilayer","dielectric-interface","view-weight"],"summary":"Aragonite tablets separated by protein sheets. Pearl luster is multilayer Bragg interference plus a dielectric Fresnel envelope, not a pearlescent flag.","phenomena":["multilayer-interference","view-dependent-color","dielectric-fresnel"],"fields":[{"id":"tablet-orientation","kind":"angle","unit":"rad","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"lamellar-tilt","frequency":1.6},"range":[-0.18,0.18]},{"id":"tablet-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","domain":"surface","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"fbm","octaves":3,"frequency":6},"range":[300,600]}],"parameters":[{"id":"n-aragonite","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.65},{"id":"n-protein","kind":"ior-real","unit":"dimensionless","value":1.4},{"id":"protein-thickness","kind":"thickness","unit":"nm","value":20},{"id":"layer-count","kind":"count","unit":"dimensionless","value":180,"range":[40,400]},{"id":"view-exp","kind":"weight","unit":"dimensionless","value":3.2},{"id":"view-lobe","kind":"lobe","unit":"enum","enum":"grazing"},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"enum","enum":"D65"},{"id":"observer","kind":"observer","unit":"enum","enum":"CIE-1931-2deg"}],"nodes":[{"id":"stack","operator":"multilayer-interference","bind":{"layerCount":{"param":"layer-count"},"thicknessA":{"field":"tablet-thickness"},"thicknessB":{"param":"protein-thickness"},"nA":{"param":"n-aragonite"},"nB":{"param":"n-protein"},"orientation":{"field":"tablet-orientation"}}},{"id":"interface","operator":"fresnel-dielectric","bind":{"ior":{"param":"n-aragonite"}}},{"id":"view","operator":"view-dependent-weight","bind":{"exponent":{"param":"view-exp"},"lobe":{"param":"view-lobe"}}},{"id":"display","operator":"spectral-integrate","bind":{"illuminant":{"param":"illuminant"},"observer":{"param":"observer"}}}],"graph":{"output":"display","edges":[{"from":"stack","to":"view"},{"from":"interface","to":"view"},{"from":"view","to":"display"}]},"evaluation":{"illuminant":"D65","observer":"CIE-1931-2deg"}},{"id":"nebula","version":"0.1.0","title":"Nebula","taxonomyIds":["scattering","emission","absorption"],"summary":"Low-density participating medium with mixed phase, dust absorption, and spectral line emission. Same volume operators as cloud; emission and spectral peaks do the rest.","phenomena":["henyey-greenstein","volume-emission","spectral-absorption"],"fields":[{"id":"gas-density","kind":"density","unit":"kg/m3","domain":"volume","source":{"type":"procedural","generator":"worley","octaves":4,"frequency":0.9},"range":[0,0.12]},{"id":"line-emission","kind":"spectral-power","unit":"W/m3/sr/nm","domain":"spectral","source":{"type":"analytic","generator":"spectral-peak","peaksNm":[486.1,500.7,656.3],"bandwidthNm":6},"range":[0,4],"notes":"Hβ, [O III], Hα — line list is data, not a nebula operator."}],"parameters":[{"id":"sigma-s","kind":"scattering-coeff","unit":"1/m","value":0.35},{"id":"sigma-a","kind":"extinction","unit":"1/m","value":0.18},{"id":"phase","kind":"phase-function","unit":"enum","enum":"hg"},{"id":"g","kind":"anisotropy","unit":"dimensionless","value":0.35},{"id":"illuminant","kind":"illuminant","unit":"